            "attributes": {
              "subtype": "qualification"
            },
            "formats": [
              "prose"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "The covalent radius can depend slightly on the type of bond:",
            "start": 1227,
            "end": 1287
          },
          {
            "id": "p18",
            "category": "CAVEAT",
            "attributes": {
              "subtype": "qualification"
            },
            "formats": [
              "list",
              "prose"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "- A **single bond** is longer, so it gives a larger radius.",
            "start": 1288,
            "end": 1347
          },
          {
            "id": "p19",
            "category": "CAVEAT",
            "attributes": {
              "subtype": "qualification"
            },
            "formats": [
              "list",
              "prose"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "- A **double bond** is shorter.",
            "start": 1348,
            "end": 1379
          },
          {
            "id": "p20",
            "category": "CAVEAT",
            "attributes": {
              "subtype": "qualification"
            },
            "formats": [
              "list",
              "prose"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "- A **triple bond** is even shorter.",
            "start": 1380,
            "end": 1416
          },
          {
            "id": "p21",
            "category": "EXAMPLE",
            "attributes": {},
            "formats": [
              "prose"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "For example, carbon has a slightly smaller effective radius in a triple bond than in a single bond because the atoms are pulled closer together.",
            "start": 1418,
            "end": 1562
          }
        ],
        "accuracy": {
          "verdict": "accurate",
          "reason": "Accurately explains that bond order shortens internuclear distance, resulting in smaller effective covalent radii for multiple bonds.",
          "errors": []
